WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.040
The FBI shut down "Silk Road",

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.000
the online drug site.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.820
They called that a major victory

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.200
over drug abuse.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.900
Silk Road generated more than a

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:09.960
billion dollars

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.080
in illegal business.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.820
The most sophisticated and extensive

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:13.980
criminal marketplace

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.669
on the internet today.

00:00:15.669 --> 00:00:16.544
Because people

00:00:16.544 --> 00:00:18.855
bought drugs on the site anonymously,

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.600
Silk Road's founder had bragged

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.000
"the state is unable to

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.360
get its thieving

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.120
murderous

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.640
mitts on it."

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.080
But he slipped up.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.980
He accidentally used his real name,

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:29.932
Ross Ulbricht,

00:00:29.932 --> 00:00:31.360
on an internet forum,

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:33.210
and the state found him.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.740
The FBI has arrested the reputed mastermind

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.500
of a popular online black market for drugs.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.980
Then judge Katherine Forrest said

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.700
because “Silk Road was a black market

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.880
of unprecedented scope"

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.572
she would sentence Ulbricht

00:00:46.572 --> 00:00:47.700
to life in prison,

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.960
with no possibility of parole,

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:50.720
ever.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:55.580
He said, "Mom, it's a death sentence. It just takes longer. "

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.700
And he's right.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:00.000
This is for all non-violent charges.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.140
She and others say

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.680
it was unfair to lock Ross up forever

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.680
for a non-violent crime.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.040
But why should we care?

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.970
Who was Ulbricht, anyway?

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.940
He seemed nice enough.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.253
"Pretty sure I want to start a family

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.320
in the next five years.”

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.240
As a kid, he was a quiet nerd,

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.742
then an Eagle Scout,

00:01:19.742 --> 00:01:21.620
excited to go to college.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.520
But in college, he became

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:24.880
a libertarian.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:25.700
And he wrote,

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.692
“I want to use economic theory

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.140
as a means to

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:31.080
abolish the use of coercion...”

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.380
Coercion, meaning force.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.900
He viewed laws against drugs as coercion...

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.400
force that stops peaceful

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.240
people from

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.580
living the way they want.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.080
"Show me your hands!”

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.480
He was right, but

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:45.680
many Americans hate and fear

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:46.820
drug use.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.536
You’re breaking up the social fabric

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.480
of our country.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.020
They applauded when the judge announced

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:52.272
Ross would be in jail

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.100
forever.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.440
This is a judge that finally got it right.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:55.080
Right.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.020
Alright, we all agree here,

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.240
life in prison without parole?

00:01:58.240 --> 00:01:58.740
Yep.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:01:59.280
Anybody else?

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.720
Any other wise guys want to do it,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.880
that’s what you're gonna get.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.127
Give me a break.

00:02:03.127 --> 00:02:05.040
Prison without parole is

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.080
not going to stop the sale of drugs.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.280
We should have learned that from

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:13.099
America’s attempt at alcohol prohibition.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.260
Once you’re an adult,

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.920
if you want to buy intoxicants,

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:16.820
it should be

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:17.840
your right.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.100
Where that’s legal,

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:19.877
sales are done

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:21.220
without violence,

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:22.500
and the products sold

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.640
are safer.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:26.240
This is your brain on drugs.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.340
Yes, many drugs are dangerous.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.640
Some who bought drugs on Silk Road

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:31.300
died.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.740
At least six people died.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:35.520
His mother said non-violent guy,

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.320
no

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.520
no.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.540
Silk Road had some rules at least,

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.600
like nothing that harmed or defrauded.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:42.640
No child pornography

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.520
was allowed.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.660
But now that the government's closed Silk Road,

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.680
replacing the site with this notice,

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.054
other illegal sites have opened,

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:50.880
and they offer

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.340
more drugs.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:54.000
These other sites, I've heard

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.871
that they're just open season, anything.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.400
So they're actually worse

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.700
and

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.140
multiple times bigger.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.720
She’d actually never seen them, so

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.860
we used the web browser Tor

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:05.349
to show them to her.

00:03:05.349 --> 00:03:07.420
It's not like they got rid of these things.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.100
Here's another one.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:08.700
Hardly.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.080
And by the way, Silk Road had 12,000 listings

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:11.920
when

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:12.940
it was taken down.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:15.140
The new sites offer more than 100,000.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:17.360
So I guess they weren't scared by Ross's

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:18.360
life sentence

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.440
as the judge said.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.260
But law enforcement keeps bragging

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.060
about successes.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:25.550
The dark net is not a place to hide.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:27.440
Here’s Attorney General Sessions announcing

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.600
that they’d shut down

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:29.820
another website.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.920
We will use every tool we have

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.280
to stop criminals from exploiting

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.140
vulnerable people.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:37.760
But the shut downs hardly make a difference.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.260
New sites appear.

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:40.160
Our critics will say

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.900
as we shutter one site,

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.892
another site emerges

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.560
and they may be right,

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:47.900
but that is the nature of criminal work.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.340
It never goes away.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:50.120
Never,

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.080
ever.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.460
Heroin,

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.560
heroin.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:55.520
So they didn't stop anything.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:56.500
No, they actually,

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.540
there was a spike after the sentence was given.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.140
It had the opposite effect.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:01.020
It’s a

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:02.340
travesty,

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.240
what’s going on.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.740
Still, I find it hard

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:06.100
to support her son since

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.680
he was also accused

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.240
of trying to kill people.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.440
A murder for hire plot.

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:12.580
Trying to hire a hit man.

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:15.320
It's completely digital evidence and hearsay basically

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.520
by the government.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.220
Ulbricht suspects an undercover cop

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:19.979
planted those messages.

00:04:19.979 --> 00:04:20.694
A mortgage company

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.320
will not take a screen shot

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.460
of a bank statement

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:24.580
because they know

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:25.990
how easily faked it is.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:27.800
No one was actually killed,

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.720
and the government didn’t charge Ulbricht

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:30.900
with murder-for-hire

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.100
in his trial.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.240
Let's just say

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:34.660
for argument's sake,

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:36.080
that everything is true.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.500
The typical for sentence for murder-for-hire

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.480
when there is no murder

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.280
because there were no murders

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:40.820
to be clear,

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:43.580
is 10 years.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.780
Double life, plus 40 years

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:47.180
without parole

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.100
for a young guy who

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.340
you know, was a zealot.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:52.820
He was a libertarian,

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:54.460
he believed in free markets

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.040
and volunteerism.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:57.680
He's not a dangerous person.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:59.060
No American is safer

00:04:59.060 --> 00:04:59.820
because

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.000
Ross Ulbricht is in

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.180
jail for life.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:04.100
He's just one more casualty

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:05.600
of our failing drug war.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:08.360
Drug dealers shoot each other,

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:09.340
shoot bystanders,

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:10.140
and corrupt

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:11.480
whole neighborhoods.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.100
Police! Search warrant!

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.780
The police risk their lives

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.560
and sometimes kill innocent people.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.940
Locking up Ulbricht

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:21.080
won’t make anything better.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.460
The drug war

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:23.800
does much more harm

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.160
than any drug.

